A||N||17||bHooper||Rebuilding my baby :D||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||03-14-2000||07:47 AM||||Ok, after much thought and pain, I have found a tranny, ordering it tommorow, and have put together the following agenda to get my car back on the road.  I will try to get some photos later this week so you guys, and girls, can see what I am "begining with".<BR>Ok, here's the plan:<P><B>March:</B> purchase and install tranny, flywheel, altenator, rear main oil seal and clutch kit (I am now broke!)<BR><B>April:</B> Install new battery, tray and support... go for a drive!!!<BR><B>May:</B>  brakes, brakes, brakes, brakes... <BR><B>June:</B> Replace body, install new engine and tranny mounts<BR><B>July:</B> new bushings<BR><B>August/September:</B> Springs and Struts<BR><B>October:</B> Short shifter and dew strips<BR><B>November/December:</B> Exhaust system<BR><B>January/February/March:</B>  Paint and tires<BR><B>April:</B> time to start working on the interior... Mr Mikes Seat covers are nice<BR><B>May:</B> New headliner/carpet<P><B>June 2001:</B>  PLAYPLAYPLAYPLAY!!!!!!!<P><B>July 2001:</B>  What mods am I interested in.... hmmm a 3.2 liter conversion would be nice, but I really like the Buick 3800  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Yes this is ambitious, and done on a budget, that's why it will take so long... but it is, afterall, just a plan.... as you can see one that has already changed!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by bHooper (edited 03-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||turbo86se||03-14-2000||10:06 AM||||bhooper, looks like your Fiero will be running just in time to bring it up to FOSEVA's Fiero show in Williamsburg, VA june 15-18 this summer. I'm making every effort to attend, and I'll be driving my 86SE. If I could find someone to drive my yellow T-Top 88 coupe, you'll see that too! Hope to see you there!  -joel||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||03-14-2000||10:20 AM||||Good things take time. I've been working on the Batmobile for about 10 months and I'm a long ways from finished. Realistically, I'm looking at probably next spring for a completion date for mine too. Keep plugging away, it'll pay off. You'll have more motivation once it's running again. Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||03-14-2000||11:36 AM||||turbo... unfortunatly, my car does not have a body on it at the moment, and likely want by this june either.  so making the show in williamsburg, might be a little difficult.  of course, if you <B>really</B> need someone to drive your yellow ttop car... i could help you find someone for that job  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||03-14-2000||08:45 PM||||ok, i'm starting to have second thoughts about buying the tranny first.  it seems that the salvage yard doesnt take plastic (mc/visa), my prefered method of payment  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> and since i wasn't planning on actually putting the tranny in until late april or 1st of may, i think it is best to buy everything else i need 1st, then buy the tranny.  that way, i will still be able to exchange it if it doesnt work properly!  it's been my experience that salvage yards only offer a 5 day waranty on parts... which will have easily expired by the time i get the tranny installed! ||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||03-18-2000||01:52 PM||||Isn't it fun to change your mind about things?  I purchased a tranny, on Friday... today I am replacing the rear main oil seal, and am going to bondo over the hole where the battery used to be.<P>I will pick up the tranny on tuesday or wednesday, and plan on installing it sometime  in the next week!  Actually, by the 1st, my car should (fingers crossed) be able to move under its own power!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Motorhead||03-18-2000||04:17 PM||||I got mine mechanicly sound and running first, now I can enjoy driving the car while I amass my store of treasures in the spare bedroom.  So far, a wing,new sail panels,extra lower quarter panels for installing scoops on when I finally decide on which ones, GT wheels,and  bra, short shifter arrives this week. Gonna' go ahead and install that.<P>If I find myself getting impatiante, I sit in the spare bedroom surrounded by my stuff, and picture the car with all of it installd around the new paint job that's in the works. <P>I'm at a year, and counting.||||reg||1
